msgid "What changed in August 2026"
msgstr "2026年8月發生了什麼變化"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:389
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"Before this work, I had done a lot of manual reverse engineering. I would "
"inspect a function until I had an explanation, then test that explanation "
"against the program. Getting further meant spending more of my own time on "
"the next function. It also meant keeping an increasingly large picture in my"
" head."
msgstr ""
"在這之前，我做過很多手工逆向。我會反覆檢視一個函式，直到能解釋它，再對照程式驗證這個解釋。想推進專案，就得親自花更多時間研究下一個函式，腦子裡也要記住越來越多的整體關係。"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:396
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"Most of my RE work is on games. I reconstruct them so their behavior can be "
"understood and eventually carried into a port or a mod. That is the "
"experience behind this article. The method can be useful elsewhere, but each"
" field needs to establish what it can check against a reliable reference."
msgstr ""
"我的逆向工作主要圍繞遊戲。我希望透過重建弄清遊戲的行為，最終做出移植版或 "
"mod。這篇文章來自這些經歷。方法可以遷移到其他領域，但每個領域都需要先明確：什麼可以用可靠的基準來驗證。"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:403
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"In August 2026, I started exploring agent-driven RE seriously. I wanted to "
"see how far an agent could get with access to the program and ordinary "
"development tools. Touhou reconstruction gave me a substantial project in "
"which to find out."
msgstr ""
"2026 年 8 月，我開始認真探索讓程式設計助手做逆向。有了程式本身和常用開發工具，它究竟能走多遠？東方遊戲重建給了我一個足夠完整的專案來尋找答案。"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:409
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"The early progress was startling. An investigation could keep moving without"
" me choosing every individual step. A failed comparison might send the agent"
" to another caller. It could write a small diagnostic and use the result to "
"decide what to try next. Giving it that freedom made a difference: I could "
"spend more attention on the project's direction and on whether its checks "
"were trustworthy."
msgstr ""
"早期的進展讓我吃驚。我不再需要為每一步作選擇，調查也能持續推進。對比失敗後，助手可能轉去檢視另一個呼叫方，寫一段診斷程式，再根據結果決定下一步。這種自主性改變了我的工作：我可以更多關注專案方向，以及檢查是否可靠。"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:418
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"The pace got my attention first. Then I began wondering what would survive "
"beyond the current project. Would the next game benefit from everything we "
"had just learned?"
msgstr "速度先引起了我的注意。隨後我開始想：當前專案結束後，什麼會留下來？下一個遊戲能不能用上我們剛學到的經驗？"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:425
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid "TH08: building on human work"
msgstr "TH08：接續前人的工作"

#. {ph0}: <a href="https://github.com/N0zoM1z0/th08">
#. {ph1}: </a>
#. {ph2}: <a href="https://github.com/GensokyoClub/th08" >
#. {ph3}: </a >
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:426
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"{ph0}TH08{ph1}, Imperishable Night, began as a continuation of "
"{ph2}GensokyoClub's reconstruction{ph3}. Their public source gave me a "
"substantial foundation. It came with knowledge of the build and a history of"
" contributions that I preserved in the continuation."
msgstr ""
"{ph0}TH08{ph1}，也就是《東方永夜抄》，從接續{ph2}GensokyoClub "
"的重建工作{ph3}開始。他們的公開原始碼提供了紮實的基礎，也留下了構建經驗和貢獻歷史。我在後續工作中保留了這些歷史。"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:435
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"The imported history ends at the public 10 August checkpoint. My independent"
" continuation began on 13 August. By 19 August, the ledger recorded source "
"for all 1,107 identified game functions."
msgstr ""
"匯入的歷史截至 8 月 10 日的公開檢查點。我的獨立續作從 8 月 13 日開始。到 8 月 19 日，進度臺賬中已識別的 1,107 "
"個遊戲函式都有了原始碼。"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:440
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"A playable Linux reconstruction port was committed on 24 August, roughly "
"eleven days after the continuation began. A Web edition followed. The native"
" Linux 64-bit release arrived on 30 August."
msgstr ""
"8 月 24 日，我們提交了可玩的 Linux 重建移植版，距離開始續作約十一天。隨後做出了 Web 版。8 月 30 日，原生 Linux 64 "
"位版釋出。"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:445
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"What struck me was that the work had reached a program people could run. "
"Getting there required following problems beyond an individual function. "
"Even when two functions looked correct in isolation, they could accidentally"
" use separate copies of state that should have been shared."
msgstr ""
"最打動我的是，這些工作最終變成了大家能執行的程式。為此必須解決單個函式以外的問題。即使兩個函式分別看起來都對，也可能各自使用一份本應共享的狀態。"

#. {ph0}: <strong>
#. {ph1}: </strong>
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:452
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"This made reference checks central to the work. I call them "
"{ph0}oracles{ph1}. A code comparison can tell us whether a reconstructed "
"function reproduces the original instructions. A runtime check can tell us "
"whether an exercised route reaches the expected state. The agent proposes an"
" explanation and tests it; a mismatch gives it something specific to "
"investigate."
msgstr ""
"這讓對照檢查成為工作的核心。我把這些基準稱為{ph0}驗證基準（oracle）{ph1}。程式碼對比可以檢查重建函式是否復現原始指令；執行時檢查可以確認已走過的路徑是否到達預期狀態。助手提出解釋，再驗證它。發現不匹配，就有了具體的調查方向。"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:460
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid "An exact match with the wrong constant"
msgstr "常量錯了，卻仍然“精確匹配”"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:461
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"An oracle is software someone wrote. TH08 gave me a clear reminder of how "
"much can depend on that software."
msgstr "校驗工具也是人寫的軟體。TH08 讓我清楚地看到，多少結論都依賴著它。"

#. {ph0}: <code>0.0</code>
#. {ph1}: <code>128.0</code>
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:465
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"In September, a bug reported by a downstream Switch port led back to item "
"auto-collection. The reconstructed source checked player power against "
"{ph0}. The original used {ph1}, the maximum-power threshold."
msgstr ""
"9 月，下游 Switch 移植版報告了一個 bug，最後追溯到道具自動收集。重建原始碼把玩家火力與 {ph0} 比較，而原版用的是 "
"{ph1}，即滿火力的閾值。"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:471
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"Normal power is non-negative, so the reconstructed power check was "
"effectively always satisfied. Above the collection line, the game could "
"attract items without requiring maximum power. The other exceptions in the "
"condition were correct. This one constant changed the behavior."
msgstr ""
"正常火力不會小於零，所以重建版的火力條件幾乎總是滿足。玩家到了收集線上方，不用滿火力也會吸取道具。條件裡的其他例外沒有問題，但這一個常量就改變了行為。"

#. {ph0}: <strong >
#. {ph1}: </strong >
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:478
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid "{ph0}Yet the function had already passed the exact comparison.{ph1}"
msgstr "{ph0}可這個函式之前已經透過了精確對比。{ph1}"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:484
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"A rebuild can put a constant at a different address. The comparison tool "
"accounted for that by adjusting addresses in the compiled instructions "
"before comparing them with the original. But it never checked the floating-"
"point value stored at the referenced address."
msgstr ""
"重新編譯後，常量可能出現在不同地址。比較工具會先調整編譯後指令中的地址，再和原版比較，以處理這種差異。問題是，它從未檢查被引用地址中實際存放的浮點值。"

#. {ph0}: <code>128.0</code>
#. {ph1}: <code>0.0</code>
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:491
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"That left a hole in the check. It could point the reconstructed instruction "
"at the original's {ph0} while the source still said {ph1}. The instruction "
"bytes matched. The source meant something different."
msgstr "漏洞就在這裡：工具可以把重建指令的引用地址調整為原版的 {ph0}，而原始碼裡寫的仍然是 {ph1}。指令位元組匹配了，原始碼含義卻不同。"

#. {ph0}: <a href="https://github.com/N0zoM1z0/th08/pull/11" >
#. {ph1}: </a >
#. {ph2}: <a href="https://github.com/N0zoM1z0/th08/pull/13">
#. {ph3}: </a>
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:497
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"The {ph0}2 September fix{ph1} corrected the source and made the comparison "
"check the referenced constant's actual bytes. A {ph2}wider audit{ph3} then "
"examined 1,548 floating-literal references. It found another twelve "
"incorrect references across five accepted functions."
msgstr ""
"{ph0}9 月 2 日的修復{ph1}糾正了原始碼，並讓比較工具檢查被引用常量的實際位元組。隨後進行的{ph2}全面審計{ph3}檢查了 1,548 "
"處浮點常量引用，又在五個已透過驗收的函式中發現十二處錯誤引用。"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:508
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"The comparison now checks every such floating literal. Its tests include "
"deliberately wrong values to make sure they are rejected. We also had to "
"revisit results that had passed the weaker check."
msgstr "現在工具會檢查每一處這樣的浮點常量。測試還會故意使用錯誤值，確保工具能夠拒絕它們。我們也重新檢查了曾經透過舊版檢查的結果。"

#. {ph0}: <strong>
#. {ph1}: </strong>
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:513
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"{ph0}The oracle needed reconstructing too.{ph1} Repairing it was part of "
"repairing the game."
msgstr "{ph0}驗證基準本身也需要重建。{ph1}修復它，就是修復遊戲的一部分。"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:517
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"That matters when the team is mostly one person working with agents. I "
"cannot personally inspect every line they produce, so much of my confidence "
"rests on their checks. A shared oracle's blind spot can affect many "
"investigations before I notice it. I have to understand what the checker "
"actually verifies and test it against cases that ought to fail."
msgstr ""
"當團隊幾乎就是一個人加一群程式設計助手時，這一點尤其重要。我無法逐行檢查它們寫出的所有程式碼，很多信心都來自檢查結果。共享驗證基準中的盲點，可能在我發現之前就影響許多調查。我必須弄清工具到底驗證了什麼，再用應當失敗的案例測試它。"

#. {ph0}: <strong >
#. {ph1}: </strong >
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:525
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"As the work continued, those checks became part of the repository. So did "
"the reasons for source changes and notes that let a later session pick up "
"where an earlier one stopped. {ph0}The repository was becoming the project's"
" working memory.{ph1}"
msgstr ""
"隨著專案推進，檢查程式進入了程式碼儲存庫。原始碼修改的理由也儲存在裡面，還有讓下一次會話能夠接著做的記錄。{ph0}程式碼儲存庫正在成為專案的工作記憶。{ph1}"

#. {ph0}: <strong >
#. {ph1}: </strong >
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:534
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"{ph0}A successful batch gave us both recovered code and a better environment"
" for the next batch.{ph1}"
msgstr "{ph0}每完成一批工作，我們既得到了還原的程式碼，也改善了下一批工作的環境。{ph1}"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:542
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid "Two different ideas of reconstruction"
msgstr "兩種不同的重建理念"

#. {ph0}: <a
#. href="https://web.archive.org/web/20260909051514/https://github.com/GensokyoClub/th08#important-
#. notice" >
#. {ph1}: </a >
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:543
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"GensokyoClub's {ph0}public README{ph1} makes its disagreement with this kind"
" of work explicit. The notice announces that further development will happen"
" privately until completion. One passage reads:"
msgstr ""
"GensokyoClub 的{ph0}公開 "
"README{ph1}明確表達了對這種工作的異議。公告說，專案完成前，後續開發將在私下進行。其中有這樣一段話："

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:554
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"The rise of grifters (AI decompilations and ports) in this space taking from"
" our work paints a bad image for future decompilation efforts…"
msgstr "“這個領域裡出現了利用我們成果的投機者（AI 反編譯和移植專案），給未來的反編譯工作留下了不好的印象……”"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:560
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"The notice also describes the psychological toll on the maintainers. Their "
"contribution policy excludes pull requests produced primarily with AI. They "
"have put their free time into difficult work, and that work helped make my "
"continuation possible. I respect the effort behind it. The disagreement I "
"want to discuss is about how reconstruction should proceed and how a "
"contribution should be judged."
msgstr ""
"公告也提到了維護者承受的心理壓力。他們的貢獻政策不接受主要由 AI 生成的 "
"PR。他們用業餘時間投入了艱難的工作，這些成果讓我的續作成為可能。我尊重他們付出的努力。我想討論的分歧，是重建應當如何推進，以及貢獻應當如何評價。"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:569
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"In the manual workflow I knew, developing an understanding of a function and"
" reconstructing it usually fell to the same person. A project relied heavily"
" on that person's expertise. Trust in the contributor mattered because so "
"much of the reasoning happened while they worked."
msgstr ""
"在我熟悉的手工流程中，理解一個函式和重建它，通常由同一個人完成。專案非常依賴這個人的專業能力。很多推理發生在工作過程中，所以對貢獻者本人的信任很重要。"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:576
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"Existing projects already preserve knowledge in their source and build "
"tools. What changed for me was that an agent could use that knowledge to "
"pursue the next investigation on its own."
msgstr "已有專案本就會在原始碼和構建工具中儲存知識。對我而言，變化在於：程式設計助手能利用這些知識，自主推進下一次調查。"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:581
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"In my continuation, I decide the objective and the standard for accepting a "
"result. The agent has broad freedom to investigate. Its proposed "
"reconstruction then has to survive the relevant checks. I want another "
"person to be able to examine why we chose an implementation, even if an "
"agent did most of the work."
msgstr ""
"在我的續作中，我來確定目標和驗收標準，助手有充分的調查自由。它提出的重建方案必須透過相應檢查。我希望其他人能夠看懂我們為什麼選擇這個實現，即使大部分工作由助手完成。"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:588
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"This can be a difficult transition. Years of careful work may become the "
"foundation for a continuation that moves much faster. That raises real "
"questions about credit. It also changes what maintainers need to know before"
" accepting a contribution."
msgstr ""
"這可能是一個艱難的轉變。多年的細緻工作，可能成為一個推進得更快的續作的基礎。這會帶來真實的歸屬與署名問題，也改變維護者在接受貢獻前需要了解的事情。"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:594
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"The industrial analogy helps me think about this. In a craft, much of the "
"process depends on the skill of the person carrying it out. Machinery "
"changes where that skill is needed. Someone still has to design the process "
"and recognize when its output is wrong. Different communities can choose how"
" much of that change they want to take on."
msgstr ""
"工業化的比喻有助於理解這一點。手工作業的過程往往依賴操作者的技藝。機器改變了這些技藝發揮作用的位置，但仍然需要人設計流程、識別錯誤產出。不同社群可以選擇接受多少這樣的變化。"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:602
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"My choice is to continue openly, with the inherited work credited and its "
"history preserved. I want the new work to be reviewable. That gives us a way"
" to ask how far this approach can go and to learn from what goes wrong along"
" the way."
msgstr "我的選擇是公開繼續，註明繼承的工作並保留其歷史。我希望新工作可以被審查。這樣，我們才能探索這種方法能走多遠，也從沿途的問題中學習。"

#. {ph0}: <a
#. href="https://github.com/GensokyoClub/th08/blob/e874b98e210b3be1ed21c5e03d54b883eac5069c/README.md#important-
#. notice" >
#. {ph1}: </a >
#. {ph2}: <a
#. href="https://github.com/GensokyoClub/th08/blob/f345c7dee07b849f2ff93a0029ab5ede126bf12c/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md"
#. >
#. {ph3}: </a >
#. {ph4}: <a
#. href="https://github.com/N0zoM1z0/th08/blob/d2a00f4acb4a13916e07a00bd13f714961714628/README.md#credits-
#. and-provenance" >
#. {ph5}: </a >
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:608
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"Source: GensokyoClub's {ph0}README notice{ph1}, checked on 10 October 2026, "
"and its {ph2}contribution policy{ph3}. The quotation is a shortened excerpt."
" TH08's {ph4}credits and provenance{ph5} record the continuation boundary."
msgstr ""
"來源：GensokyoClub 的{ph0}README 公告{ph1}（於 2026 年 10 月 10 "
"日核對）及其{ph2}貢獻政策{ph3}。上面的引文為節選譯文。TH08 的{ph4}貢獻署名與來源記錄{ph5}說明了獨立續作的起點。"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:626
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid "TH095: experience starts compounding"
msgstr "TH095：經驗開始產生複利"

#. {ph0}: <a href="https://github.com/N0zoM1z0/th095">
#. {ph1}: </a>
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:627
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"{ph0}TH095{ph1}, Shoot the Bullet, made the value of that experience much "
"easier to see. Its repository began on 29 August with zero confirmed game "
"functions in the ledger. We still had to learn the game. But we already knew"
" much more about how to begin a reconstruction and how to keep it moving."
msgstr ""
"{ph0}TH095{ph1}，也就是《東方文花帖》，讓這些經驗的價值更容易看清。儲存庫於 8 月 29 "
"日建立，當時臺賬中確認的遊戲函式數量為零。我們仍需研究遊戲本身，但已經更清楚如何開始重建，以及怎樣持續推進。"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:635
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"By 7 September, all 697 identified game functions had source. By 8 "
"September, 696 had been accepted as exact comparisons. The whole program "
"linked on 9 September. The Windows i386 reconstruction was marked playable "
"on 10 September, about twelve days after initialization."
msgstr ""
"到 9 月 7 日，全部 697 個已識別遊戲函式都有了原始碼。9 月 8 日，其中 696 個透過了精確對比。9 月 9 日，整個程式完成連結。9 月"
" 10 日，Windows i386 重建版被記錄為可玩，距離初始化約十二天。"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:642
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"I found this more exciting than the first project's speed. A fresh target "
"could benefit from work done on another game. The experience was already "
"present in the tools and in the way the project was organized."
msgstr "這比第一個專案的速度更讓我興奮。新目標能受益於另一個遊戲的工作。經驗已經進入工具，也進入了專案的組織方式。"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:648
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"For example, TH08 had taught us to pay attention to the assembled program "
"early. If several recovered functions depend on the same state, their "
"isolated comparisons leave an important question open. We need to see them "
"working together. That lesson helped shape how we approached TH095's whole-"
"program build."
msgstr ""
"例如，TH08 教會我們儘早關注整個程式。如果幾個還原函式依賴同一份狀態，分別對比它們仍然會留下一個關鍵問題：它們能否一起正常工作？這條經驗影響了 "
"TH095 的整程式構建方式。"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:655
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"A lesson that stays in my head is useful while I am there. Once it becomes a"
" check that another session can run, it can keep helping after I have moved "
"on. The next agent can use the result without repeating the investigation "
"that led to it."
msgstr ""
"經驗只記在我腦子裡，我在場時它才有用。變成其他會話能執行的檢查後，即使我離開，它仍能幫助專案。下一個助手可以利用檢查結果，不用重複當初得出這條經驗的調查。"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:661
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"The floating-literal bug belongs in that memory too. It explains why "
"checking a reference also requires checking the data behind it. Keeping that"
" correction with the code helps later projects avoid inheriting the old "
"check's blind spot."
msgstr ""
"浮點常量的 bug 也屬於這份記憶。它說明，檢查引用時，還要檢查引用背後的資料。把修正儲存在程式碼旁邊，可以幫助後續專案避免繼承舊工具的盲點。"

#. {ph0}: <strong >
#. {ph1}: </strong >
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:667
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"{ph0}The method becomes part of the starting material for the next "
"game.{ph1} We can spend more of the next project's effort on what is "
"actually new about its target."
msgstr "{ph0}方法本身成了下一個遊戲的起始材料。{ph1}我們可以把更多精力放在新目標真正不同的地方。"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:675
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"The same benefit is available to people joining later. They can inspect a "
"decision and rerun its check before continuing the work. They do not have to"
" reconstruct the entire project's history to find out why the source looks "
"the way it does."
msgstr "後來加入的人也能受益。他們可以檢視某個決定，重新執行檢查，再繼續工作。不用先重走整個專案的歷史，才能理解原始碼為何這樣寫。"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:683
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid "TH04: the workflow survives a different architecture"
msgstr "TH04：換了架構，工作方式仍然適用"

#. {ph0}: <a href="https://github.com/N0zoM1z0/th04">
#. {ph1}: </a>
#. {ph2}: <a href="https://github.com/nmlgc/ReC98">
#. {ph3}: </a>
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:684
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"{ph0}TH04{ph1}, Lotus Land Story, took this work into the PC-98 DOS era. The"
" target was now a 16-bit environment with four cooperating programs. "
"Understanding its hardware behavior required different evidence from the "
"Windows games. Existing {ph2}ReC98 work{ph3} gave us valuable knowledge and "
"source material here too."
msgstr ""
"{ph0}TH04{ph1}，也就是《東方幻想鄉》，把這套工作帶到了 PC-98 DOS 時代。這次是一個由四個程式協作的 16 "
"位環境。理解硬體行為，需要和 Windows 遊戲不同的證據。已有的{ph2}ReC98 工作{ph3}同樣提供了寶貴的知識與原始碼材料。"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:693
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"The DOS reconstruction is now working. In my manual testing, I played "
"complete Normal routes through their endings and checked saves. The current "
"work is a native 64-bit port. Establishing a working DOS version first gives"
" that port a reference."
msgstr ""
"DOS 重建版現在已經能執行。我手工打完了完整的 Normal 路線，看到結局，並檢查了存檔。目前正在做原生 64 位移植。先得到一個正常工作的 DOS"
" 版，就為移植提供了參照。"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:699
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"The architecture changed what we needed to investigate. It also changed the "
"compiler and runtime against which we checked our work. But the agent could "
"still follow a question through to a result and let that result guide the "
"next experiment."
msgstr "架構改變了要調查的問題，也改變了用來驗證的編譯器和執行時。但助手依然能沿著問題找到結果，再用結果指導下一次實驗。"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:705
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"Consider the transition from gameplay to an ending. We need to know what "
"state carries across that boundary and which program is responsible for it. "
"That is something we can investigate against the DOS product. Once the "
"evidence and checks are available, an agent can work through the question "
"much as it did on a Windows title."
msgstr ""
"比如從遊戲過程切換到結局：哪些狀態需要跨越這個邊界？哪個程式負責它們？我們可以對照 DOS 原版調查。只要證據和檢查可用，助手就能像研究 Windows"
" 遊戲一樣推進這個問題。"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:713
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"This is why TH04 matters to the argument. A substantial platform change did "
"not force us to start over with a new way of working. The architecture "
"defined the problem; the workflow still gave us a way to solve it."
msgstr "這就是 TH04 對這篇文章的意義。大幅的平臺變化，並沒有迫使我們重新發明一套工作方式。架構決定了問題，工作流程仍然提供瞭解決問題的方法。"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:719
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"For the 64-bit port, we can now examine the new implementation against "
"behavior already recovered on DOS. The knowledge from reconstruction gives "
"the port something to build on."
msgstr "做 64 位移植時，我們可以把新實現與 DOS 上已經還原的行為對照。重建得到的知識為移植提供了基礎。"

#. {ph0}: <a
#. href="https://github.com/N0zoM1z0/th04/blob/bb9faca54e2eb3c0d6c757c75d59ac29d2cd5e93/docs/RE_HANDOFF.md"
#. >
#. {ph1}: </a >
#. {ph2}: <a href="https://github.com/N0zoM1z0/th04/tree/port/modern-64" >
#. {ph3}: </a >
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:724
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"Project state as of 10 October 2026: {ph0}DOS reconstruction and manual "
"testing{ph1} · {ph2}64-bit port{ph3}. The port remains in development."
msgstr "截至 2026 年 10 月 10 日：{ph0}DOS 重建與手工測試{ph1} · {ph2}64 位移植{ph3}。移植仍在開發中。"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:737
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid "From exact code to readable code"
msgstr "從精確還原到可讀原始碼"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:738
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"Once a reconstruction works, I want someone else to be able to understand "
"it."
msgstr "重建版能執行之後，我還希望別人能讀懂它。"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:742
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"To me, assembly and raw offsets can feel like old friends. I realise this is"
" a slightly unusual definition of “readable.” Most people would prefer to "
"follow the game's logic without keeping the executable's memory layout in "
"their head."
msgstr ""
"對我而言，彙編和原始偏移就像老朋友。我知道，這種“可讀”的定義有點特別。多數人更希望直接看懂遊戲邏輯，而不用在腦中記住可執行檔案的記憶體佈局。"

#. {ph0}: <strong>
#. {ph1}: </strong>
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:748
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"That is where {ph0}semantic reconstruction{ph1} comes in. A recovered field "
"may still be known mainly by its offset. We follow how the game uses it "
"until we can explain its role. Then we can give it a meaningful name and a "
"type that fits the evidence. We keep the reasoning with the source so the "
"next person can see where that interpretation came from."
msgstr ""
"這就需要{ph0}語義重建{ph1}。一個還原欄位可能仍然只有偏移作為標識。我們追蹤遊戲如何使用它，直到能解釋其作用，再依據證據賦予合適的名稱和型別。推理過程和原始碼一起儲存，後來的人就能知道這個解釋從何而來。"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:756
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"This becomes especially important for a port. An absolute address tells me "
"where something lived in the old executable. It gives a 64-bit "
"implementation little help in deciding which object should own that state. "
"To move the behavior safely, we need to recover the relationship behind the "
"old memory access."
msgstr ""
"移植時，語義尤其重要。絕對地址能告訴我資料在舊程式中的位置，卻很難幫助 64 "
"位實現決定哪個物件應當持有這份狀態。要正確遷移行為，就得還原舊記憶體訪問背後的關係。"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:763
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid "The order I now use is:"
msgstr "我現在採用這樣的順序："

#. {ph0}: <strong>
#. {ph1}: </strong>
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:765
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"{ph0}Recover an exact baseline.{ph1} Compile the reconstructed pieces with "
"the historical compiler. Compare the relevant code and data with the "
"original executable. Record unresolved differences so the next phase has a "
"clear starting point."
msgstr ""
"{ph0}先建立精確還原的基線。{ph1}用當年的編譯器編譯重建程式碼，與原始可執行檔案對比相關程式碼和資料。記錄尚未解決的差異，讓下一階段有明確的起點。"

#. {ph0}: <strong>
#. {ph1}: </strong>
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:772
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"{ph0}Build and play it on the original platform.{ph1} Link those pieces into"
" the real program using the original architecture and compiler. Exercise "
"important gameplay paths. This is where we can find problems with shared "
"state or initialization that an isolated function comparison missed."
msgstr ""
"{ph0}在原平臺上構建，並實際遊玩。{ph1}用原架構和編譯器把各部分連結為真正的程式，走過重要的遊戲路徑。這能發現單函式對比漏掉的共享狀態或初始化問題。"

#. {ph0}: <strong >
#. {ph1}: </strong >
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:779
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"{ph0}Reconstruct the semantics against both references.{ph1} Take one "
"coherent part of the game at a time and establish what its recovered source "
"means. Improve its representation while preserving the exact comparisons and"
" the playable historical build."
msgstr ""
"{ph0}對照兩套基準做語義重建。{ph1}每次處理遊戲中一個完整、連貫的部分，明確還原原始碼的含義。改善程式碼表達，同時保留精確對比和可玩的原平臺構建。"

#. {ph0}: <strong>
#. {ph1}: </strong>
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:788
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"{ph0}Make the modern port.{ph1} Move the established behavior into the new "
"environment, such as a native 64-bit build. The reconstructed original-"
"platform game remains a reference for comparing how the port behaves."
msgstr "{ph0}再做現代平臺移植。{ph1}把已經確定的行為帶入新環境，例如原生 64 位構建。原平臺重建版繼續作為比較移植行為的參照。"

#. {ph0}: <strong>
#. {ph1}: </strong>
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:795
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"The playable build from the second stage becomes a {ph0}second oracle{ph1} "
"during the third. The first oracle checks whether our changed source still "
"reproduces the relevant original code and data. The second checks that the "
"reconstructed program still builds and behaves correctly along the paths we "
"exercise."
msgstr ""
"第二階段的可玩構建，在第三階段成為{ph0}第二套驗證基準{ph1}。第一套檢查修改後的原始碼是否仍然復現原版相關程式碼和資料；第二套檢查重建程式是否能構建，並在實際測試的路徑上保持正確行為。"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:803
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"They catch different mistakes. A type change can alter the generated "
"instructions. An ownership change can leave two parts of the game using "
"different copies of state. Keeping both checks available gives the agent a "
"concrete failure to investigate before carrying a refactor further."
msgstr ""
"它們能發現不同型別的錯誤。型別修改可能改變生成的指令。狀態歸屬的修改，可能讓遊戲的兩部分各自使用一份狀態。保留兩套檢查，助手就能在繼續重構之前，針對具體的失敗展開調查。"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:810
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"A name needs evidence of its own. An exact comparison cannot tell us whether"
" a field really means “invulnerability time.” We have to establish that from"
" how the game writes and uses it. If the meaning remains uncertain, a "
"neutral name is more helpful to the next reader than a confident guess."
msgstr ""
"命名也需要自己的證據。精確對比不能證明某欄位一定是“無敵時間”。我們必須從遊戲如何寫入和使用它來確認。如果含義仍不明確，中性名稱比自信的猜測更有利於下一位讀者。"

#. {ph0}: <a href="https://github.com/N0zoM1z0/touhou-reconstruction-
#. factory/blob/717e1b8560783ed17a39fdf159d30aa16bb307a7/docs/semantic-
#. reconstruction.md" >
#. {ph1}: </a >
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:817
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"We learned this order through the projects. TH08 already had playable ports "
"before some of its later historical-platform audits. That made certain "
"defects harder to see. The {ph0}Factory's current workflow{ph1} puts the "
"original-platform build first, so semantic work can use it as a reference "
"before porting begins."
msgstr ""
"這個順序來自專案中的教訓。TH08 在後來的一些原平臺審計之前，就已經有了可玩的移植版，一些缺陷因此更難察覺。{ph0}Factory "
"目前的工作流程{ph1}把原平臺構建放在前面，讓語義重建先有參照，再開始移植。"

#. {ph0}: <strong >
#. {ph1}: </strong >
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:828
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"{ph0}Exact reconstruction gives us a reference. Semantic reconstruction "
"makes the recovered knowledge usable.{ph1} A port can then build on both."
msgstr "{ph0}精確重建提供基準，語義重建讓還原的知識可用。{ph1}移植隨後建立在兩者之上。"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:837
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid "What makes this an industrial shift"
msgstr "為什麼這是工業化的轉變"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:838
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"These projects changed where I spent my attention. Once agents could carry "
"much of an investigation forward, improving their working environment became"
" one of the most useful things I could do. A better tool could help with "
"every later function that needed it."
msgstr ""
"這些專案改變了我投入注意力的地方。助手能自主推進大部分調查之後，改善它們的工作環境，就成了我最值得做的事情之一。一項工具的改進，可以幫助之後所有需要它的函式。"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:845
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"Autonomy matters here. The useful next step often becomes clear only after a"
" failed experiment. An agent needs enough freedom to follow that result "
"somewhere unexpected. If it has to wait for me to prescribe each step, much "
"of the work remains tied to my attention."
msgstr ""
"自主性在這裡很重要。下一步該怎麼做，常常在實驗失敗後才清楚。助手需要足夠的自由，沿著結果探索意料之外的方向。如果每一步都要等我指定，大部分工作仍然綁在我的注意力上。"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:852
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"I expect the agent to make wrong hypotheses. What matters is whether we can "
"test them and learn from the result. A failed check should help it "
"understand the mistake well enough to try again. I still have to decide "
"whether the accumulated evidence supports a project milestone."
msgstr ""
"我預期助手會提出錯誤假設。關鍵是我們能否驗證它們，並從結果中學習。失敗的檢查應該幫助它理解錯誤，再次嘗試。我仍要判斷：累積的證據是否足以支援某個專案里程碑。"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:859
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"REA gives the agent access to analysis tools. A question about a function's "
"caller can lead straight into inspecting that caller. The reconstruction "
"project supplies the compiler and its own reference checks. The agent can "
"use those to test the source it proposes and see where its explanation holds"
" up."
msgstr ""
"REA "
"讓助手能夠使用分析工具。調查某函式的呼叫方時，它可以直接繼續檢查那個呼叫方。重建專案提供編譯器和自己的對照檢查。助手用它們驗證提出的原始碼，看看解釋在哪些地方成立。"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:866
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"The TH08 bug shows why those checks deserve engineering attention of their "
"own. When the same comparison is used across hundreds of functions, a gap in"
" it can spread much further than a mistake in one implementation. Testing "
"the checker improves the feedback available to all that later work."
msgstr ""
"TH08 的 bug "
"說明，檢查工具本身也值得認真工程化。相同的比較用於數百個函式時，一個漏洞的影響可能遠大於某個實現中的錯誤。測試檢查器，能改善所有後續工作得到的反饋。"

#. {ph0}: <a
#. href="https://collection.sciencemuseumgroup.org.uk/objects/co51439/watts-
#. steam-engine-indicator" >
#. {ph1}: </a >
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:873
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"The industrial analogy has a useful historical example here. Boulton and "
"Watt introduced a {ph0}steam-engine indicator in 1796{ph1} to help adjust "
"engine valves. A recording version traced pressure through the piston "
"stroke. It made the engine's internal behavior available for inspection. Our"
" comparison tools serve a similar purpose: they let us examine what the "
"machinery is doing while we improve it."
msgstr ""
"工業史中有一個合適的例子：博爾頓和瓦特在{ph0}1796 "
"年引入蒸汽機示功器{ph1}，幫助調節閥門。記錄式示功器能繪出活塞行程中的壓力變化，讓人看到機器內部的執行情況。我們的比較工具也有類似作用：改進機器時，能看清它究竟做了什麼。"

#. {ph0}: <strong >
#. {ph1}: </strong >
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:886
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"{ph0}We are in the early stages of this industrial shift.{ph1} Much of the "
"infrastructure is still immature. Agents can move faster than our checks "
"were designed to support, so the process has to develop alongside them. When"
" we find a defect in a shared tool, we have to repair it and revisit the "
"results it affected. The next project can then inherit a stronger tool."
msgstr ""
"{ph0}我們正處於這場工業化轉變的早期。{ph1}許多基礎設施還不成熟。助手推進工作的速度，可能超過原有檢查的承受能力，所以流程也要一起發展。共享工具出現缺陷時，要修好它，並重查受影響的結果。下一個專案才能繼承更可靠的工具。"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:896
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"There is also a practical limit to any one conversation. It will end before "
"a large reconstruction is finished. The repository has to make it possible "
"for another session to continue without losing the reason for the last "
"decision."
msgstr "任何一段對話都有實際的長度限制。大型重建完成之前，對話就會結束。程式碼儲存庫必須讓下一次會話能繼續工作，而不丟失上一次決定背後的理由。"

#. {ph0}: <a href="https://github.com/N0zoM1z0/touhou-reconstruction-factory"
#. >
#. {ph1}: </a >
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:902
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"The {ph0}Touhou Reconstruction Factory{ph1} grew out of that need. It gives "
"projects a shared way to carry their checks and lessons forward. Work on one"
" game can improve the starting conditions for another."
msgstr ""
"{ph0}Touhou Reconstruction "
"Factory{ph1}正是為此而建立。它提供一種共用方式，讓專案把檢查和經驗傳遞下去。一個遊戲的工作，可以改善另一個遊戲的起點。"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:912
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"That is what makes the industrial analogy meaningful to me. Experience "
"starts becoming part of tools that others can use. Improving those tools "
"changes how much the next person—or the next agent—can get done."
msgstr "這就是工業化比喻對我的意義：經驗開始進入別人也能使用的工具。改善工具，就能改變下一個人或下一個助手能完成多少工作。"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:920
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid "The projects we can now consider"
msgstr "現在值得嘗試的專案"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:921
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"The pace matters because it changes the decision to begin. A game could be "
"fascinating to reverse engineer and still demand more of my own attention "
"than I could realistically give it. Many projects would stay ideas."
msgstr "速度的意義在於，它改變了是否開始一個專案的決定。某個遊戲也許很值得逆向，卻需要我投入遠超現實所能承受的精力。很多專案因此一直停留在想法裡。"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:927
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"Now I can see a way to keep such a project moving through repeated "
"investigations. Getting a working reconstruction makes a port more "
"practical. Recovering readable semantics makes it easier for someone else to"
" explore a mod. The effort put into understanding the game can keep paying "
"off after the first version runs."
msgstr ""
"現在，我看到了透過一次次調查持續推進它們的可能。得到能執行的重建版，讓移植更可行；還原可讀的語義，讓別人更容易探索 "
"mod。理解遊戲的投入，可以在第一版執行之後繼續帶來回報。"

#. {ph0}: <strong >
#. {ph1}: </strong >
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:934
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"I now look at an unfamiliar program and ask: {ph0}what access, feedback and "
"accumulated knowledge would let an agent work on this reliably?{ph1}"
msgstr "現在看到一個陌生程式，我會問：{ph0}怎樣的工具訪問、反饋和知識積累，能讓助手可靠地推進這個專案？{ph1}"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:941
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"That question makes me consider projects I would previously have left alone."
" Each one can improve the way we approach the next. I want to keep exploring"
" how far that can take us."
msgstr "這個問題讓我考慮以前會放棄的專案。每個專案都能改善下一個專案的工作方式。我想繼續探索，這能帶我們走多遠。"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:949
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid "Project milestones and sources"
msgstr "專案里程碑與來源"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:950
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"The dates describe recorded project checkpoints, checked against public "
"GitHub history on 10 October 2026. Elapsed time is calendar time between "
"commits. Source presence, exact comparisons, a build and a runtime result "
"each name a different milestone."
